A||||0||batboy||Saw 2 nice Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||11-12-1999||11:00 PM||||Ok, this might sound a little corny, but I'm driving my black 85 GT in Topeka traffic. We are having an Indian summer here and I have all the windows down and the sunroof cracked open. I see a very nice black 86 or 87 SE in the lane next to me. We stop side by side at the next lights. This flawless little Fiero notchback absolutely gleamed and sparkled. Fresh wax job and totally detailed to the max, inside and out. I'm feeling very humbled driving my filthy, dirty Fiero that needs a paint job and the seats covers replaced. He looks over and checks out my car and gives me a nod. I tell him, "You're Fiero's looking great!" He breaks out into the huge ear to ear grin and says, "thanks." You could tell this guy was very proud of his Fiero. Pretty exceptional car.<P>Sometime last week, I was driving on the freeway through Topeka. Up ahead, I saw a extra sharp, metallic light tan colored fastback with a wing on the tail and fat tires. I speeded up and finally and pulled up next to him. He waved and gave me a thumbs up which I returned back to him. This car is another garage baby, I'm telling you this GT was ultra clean.||||reg||1
